    {
      "id": "cb6f94d2a511-q4",
      "number": 4,
      "question": "Below are two chemical equations: Zn (s) + CuSO&#8324; (aq) &rarr; ZnSO&#8324; (aq) + Cu (s) Pb (s) + CuCl&#8322; (aq) &rarr; PbCl&#8322; (aq) + Cu (s) Why does copper get separated from its compound form in both cases? &#2344;&#2368;&#2330;&#2375; &#2342;&#2379; &#2352;&#2366;&#2360;&#2366;&#2351;&#2344;&#2367;&#2325; &#2360;&#2350;&#2368;&#2325;&#2352;&#2339; &#2342;&#2367;&#2319; &#2327;&#2319; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;: Zn (s) + CuSO&#8324; (aq) &rarr; ZnSO&#8324; (aq) + Cu (s) Pb (s) + CuCl&#8322; (aq) &rarr; PbCl&#8322; (aq) + Cu (s) &#2342;&#2379;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2366;&#2350;&#2354;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2340;&#2366;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366; &#2309;&#2346;&#2344;&#2375; &#2351;&#2380;&#2327;&#2367;&#2325; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2360;&#2375; &#2309;&#2354;&#2327; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2361;&#2379; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?",
      "questionHtml": "<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Below are two chemical equations:</p><p>Zn (s) + CuSO&#8324; (aq) &rarr; ZnSO&#8324; (aq) + Cu (s)</p><p>Pb (s) + CuCl&#8322; (aq) &rarr; PbCl&#8322; (aq) + Cu (s)</p><p>Why does copper get separated from its compound form in both cases?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2344;&#2368;&#2330;&#2375; &#2342;&#2379; &#2352;&#2366;&#2360;&#2366;&#2351;&#2344;&#2367;&#2325; &#2360;&#2350;&#2368;&#2325;&#2352;&#2339; &#2342;&#2367;&#2319; &#2327;&#2319; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;:</p><p>Zn (s) + CuSO&#8324; (aq) &rarr; ZnSO&#8324; (aq) + Cu (s)</p><p>Pb (s) + CuCl&#8322; (aq) &rarr; PbCl&#8322; (aq) + Cu (s)</p><p>&#2342;&#2379;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2366;&#2350;&#2354;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2340;&#2366;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366; &#2309;&#2346;&#2344;&#2375; &#2351;&#2380;&#2327;&#2367;&#2325; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2360;&#2375; &#2309;&#2354;&#2327; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2361;&#2379; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "Zinc and Lead are unstable in element form. &#2332;&#2367;&#2306;&#2325; &#2324;&#2352; &#2360;&#2368;&#2360;&#2366; &#2340;&#2340;&#2381;&#2357; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2309;&#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Zinc and Lead are unstable in element form.</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2332;&#2367;&#2306;&#2325; &#2324;&#2352; &#2360;&#2368;&#2360;&#2366; &#2340;&#2340;&#2381;&#2357; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2309;&#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "Copper compounds break down under high pressure. &#2340;&#2366;&#2306;&#2348;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2351;&#2380;&#2327;&#2367;&#2325; &#2313;&#2330;&#2381;&#2330; &#2342;&#2348;&#2366;&#2357; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2335;&#2370;&#2335; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Copper compounds break down under high pressure.</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2340;&#2366;&#2306;&#2348;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2351;&#2380;&#2327;&#2367;&#2325; &#2313;&#2330;&#2381;&#2330; &#2342;&#2348;&#2366;&#2357; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2335;&#2370;&#2335; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "Zinc and Lead are more reactive than Copper. &#2332;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2366; &#2324;&#2352; &#2360;&#2368;&#2360;&#2366; &#2340;&#2366;&#2306;&#2348;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2369;&#2354;&#2344;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;&#2358;&#2368;&#2354; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Zinc and Lead are more reactive than Copper.</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2332;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2366; &#2324;&#2352; &#2360;&#2368;&#2360;&#2366; &#2340;&#2366;&#2306;&#2348;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2369;&#2354;&#2344;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;&#2358;&#2368;&#2354; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "Copper is more reactive than Zinc and Lead. &#2340;&#2366;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366; &#2332;&#2367;&#2306;&#2325; &#2324;&#2352; &#2360;&#2368;&#2360;&#2366; &#2360;&#2375; &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325; &#2309;&#2349;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;&#2358;&#2368;&#2354; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Copper is more reactive than Zinc and Lead.</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2340;&#2366;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366; &#2332;&#2367;&#2306;&#2325; &#2324;&#2352; &#2360;&#2368;&#2360;&#2366; &#2360;&#2375; &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325; &#2309;&#2349;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;&#2358;&#2368;&#2354; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;</span>"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "C",
      "solution": "<p>More reactive metals displace less reactive ones in displacement reactions.</p><p>&bull; A displacement reaction is a chemical reaction in which a more reactive element displaces a less reactive element from its compound.</p><p>&bull; A + BC &rarr; AC + B</p><p>&bull; Where A is more reactive than B.</p>",
