      "number": 6,
      "question": "Which of the following chemical reactions takes place when quick lime reacts with water? &#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344; &#2360;&#2368; &#2352;&#2366;&#2360;&#2366;&#2351;&#2344;&#2367;&#2325; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2340;&#2348; &#2361;&#2379;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376; &#2332;&#2348; &#2330;&#2370;&#2344;&#2366; &#2346;&#2366;&#2344;&#2368; &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?",
      "questionHtml": "<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Which of the following chemical reactions takes place when quick lime reacts with water?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344; &#2360;&#2368; &#2352;&#2366;&#2360;&#2366;&#2351;&#2344;&#2367;&#2325; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2340;&#2348; &#2361;&#2379;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376; &#2332;&#2348; &#2330;&#2370;&#2344;&#2366; &#2346;&#2366;&#2344;&#2368; &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</span>",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "CaO(s) + H&#8322;O(l) &rarr; Ca + H&#8322;(aq) CaO(s) H&#8322;O(l) &rarr; &#2360;&#2368;&#2319; &#2319;&#2330;&#8322;(&#2319;&#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2370;)",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">CaO(s) + H&#8322;O(l) &rarr; Ca + H&#8322;(aq)</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">CaO(s) H&#8322;O(l) &rarr; &#2360;&#2368;&#2319; &#2319;&#2330;&#8322;(&#2319;&#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2370;)</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "C(s) + O&#8322;(g) &rarr; CO&#8322;(g) &#2360;&#2368;(&#2319;&#2360;) &#2323;&#8322;(&#2332;&#2368;) &rarr; &#2360;&#2368;&#2323;&#8322;(&#2332;&#2368;)",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">C(s) + O&#8322;(g) &rarr; CO&#8322;(g)</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2360;&#2368;(&#2319;&#2360;) &#2323;&#8322;(&#2332;&#2368;) &rarr; &#2360;&#2368;&#2323;&#8322;(&#2332;&#2368;)</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "CaO(s) + H&#8322;O(l) &rarr; Ca(OH)&#8322;(aq) CaO(s) H&#8322;O(l) &rarr; Ca(OH)&#8322;(aq)",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">CaO(s) + H&#8322;O(l) &rarr; Ca(OH)&#8322;(aq)</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">CaO(s) H&#8322;O(l) &rarr; Ca(OH)&#8322;(aq)</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "CH&#8324; (g) + 2O&#8322; (g) &rarr; CO&#8322; (g) + 2H&#8322;O (g) &#2360;&#2368;&#2319;&#2330;&#8324; (&#2332;&#2368;) 2&#2323;&#8322; (&#2332;&#2368;) &rarr; &#2360;&#2368;&#2323;&#8322; (&#2332;&#2368;) 2&#2319;&#2330;&#8322;&#2323; (&#2332;&#2368;)",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">CH&#8324; (g) + 2O&#8322; (g) &rarr; CO&#8322; (g) + 2H&#8322;O (g)</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2360;&#2368;&#2319;&#2330;&#8324; (&#2332;&#2368;) 2&#2323;&#8322; (&#2332;&#2368;) &rarr; &#2360;&#2368;&#2323;&#8322; (&#2332;&#2368;) 2&#2319;&#2330;&#8322;&#2323; (&#2332;&#2368;)</span>"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "C",
      "solution": "<p>When quick lime (CaO) reacts with water, it forms slaked lime (Ca(OH)&#8322;) in an exothermic reaction:</p><p><i><b>CaO(s)+H<sub>2</sub>O(l) &rarr; Ca(OH)<sub>2</sub>&#8203;(aq)</b></i></p><p>This reaction is widely used in whitewashing walls.</p>",
      "images": [],
      "subject": null,
      "topic": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
    {
      "id": "cb6f94d2a511-q7",
      "number": 7,
      "question": "Who developed the theory of combustion as a chemical reaction with oxygen in the 18th century, that excluded phlogiston theory? 18&#2357;&#2368;&#2306; &#2358;&#2340;&#2366;&#2348;&#2381;&#2342;&#2368; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2321;&#2325;&#2381;&#2360;&#2368;&#2332;&#2344; &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; &#2352;&#2366;&#2360;&#2366;&#2351;&#2344;&#2367;&#2325; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2342;&#2361;&#2344; &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2367;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343;&#2366;&#2306;&#2340; &#2325;&#2379; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2360;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;, &#2332;&#2367;&#2360;&#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2347;&#2381;&#2354;&#2377;&#2332;&#2367;&#2360;&#2381;&#2335;&#2344; &#2360;&#2367;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343;&#2366;&#2306;&#2340; &#2325;&#2379; &#2358;&#2366;&#2350;&#2367;&#2354; &#2344;&#2361;&#2368;&#2306; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366;?",
      "questionHtml": "<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Who developed the theory of combustion as a chemical reaction with oxygen in the 18th century, that excluded phlogiston theory?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">18&#2357;&#2368;&#2306; &#2358;&#2340;&#2366;&#2348;&#2381;&#2342;&#2368; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2321;&#2325;&#2381;&#2360;&#2368;&#2332;&#2344; &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; &#2352;&#2366;&#2360;&#2366;&#2351;&#2344;&#2367;&#2325; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2342;&#2361;&#2344; &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2367;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343;&#2366;&#2306;&#2340; &#2325;&#2379; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2360;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;, &#2332;&#2367;&#2360;&#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2347;&#2381;&#2354;&#2377;&#2332;&#2367;&#2360;&#2381;&#2335;&#2344; &#2360;&#2367;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343;&#2366;&#2306;&#2340; &#2325;&#2379; &#2358;&#2366;&#2350;&#2367;&#2354; &#2344;&#2361;&#2368;&#2306; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366;?</span>",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "Antoine Lavoisier &#2319;&#2306;&#2335;&#2379;&#2344;&#2368; &#2354;&#2366;&#2357;&#2379;&#2311;&#2360;&#2367;&#2319;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Antoine Lavoisier</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2319;&#2306;&#2335;&#2379;&#2344;&#2368; &#2354;&#2366;&#2357;&#2379;&#2311;&#2360;&#2367;&#2319;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "Robert Boyle &#2352;&#2377;&#2348;&#2352;&#2381;&#2335; &#2348;&#2377;&#2351;&#2354;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Robert Boyle</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2352;&#2377;&#2348;&#2352;&#2381;&#2335; &#2348;&#2377;&#2351;&#2354;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "Friedrich W&#246;hler &#2347;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2337;&#2352;&#2367;&#2325; &#2357;&#2381;&#2354;&#2361;&#2354;&#2352;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Friedrich W&#246;hler</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2347;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2337;&#2352;&#2367;&#2325; &#2357;&#2381;&#2354;&#2361;&#2354;&#2352;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "Johann Becher &#2332;&#2379;&#2361;&#2366;&#2344; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2352;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Johann Becher</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2332;&#2379;&#2361;&#2366;&#2344; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2352;</span>"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "A",
      "solution": "<p>Antoine Lavoisier was a French chemist who is often called the \"Father of Modern Chemistry\". In the 18th century, he made a groundbreaking contribution to our understanding of chemical reactions, particularly combustion.</p><p>Before Lavoisier, scientists believed in the phlogiston theory, which suggested that a substance called phlogiston was released during burning. Lavoisier challenged this theory by demonstrating that combustion is actually a chemical reaction involving oxygen. He showed that when substances burn, they combine with oxygen from the air, which was a revolutionary concept at the time.</p>",
      "images": [],
      "subject": null,
      "topic": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
    {
      "id": "cb6f94d2a511-q8",
      "number": 8,
      "question": "Which gas is evolved when iron and water react? &#2354;&#2379;&#2361;&#2366; &#2324;&#2352; &#2346;&#2366;&#2344;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344; &#2360;&#2368; &#2327;&#2376;&#2360; &#2344;&#2367;&#2325;&#2354;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;?",
      "questionHtml": "<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Which gas is evolved when iron and water react?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2354;&#2379;&#2361;&#2366; &#2324;&#2352; &#2346;&#2366;&#2344;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344; &#2360;&#2368; &#2327;&#2376;&#2360; &#2344;&#2367;&#2325;&#2354;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;?</span>",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "Hydrogen &#2361;&#2366;&#2311;&#2337;&#2381;&#2352;&#2379;&#2332;&#2344;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Hydrogen</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2361;&#2366;&#2311;&#2337;&#2381;&#2352;&#2379;&#2332;&#2344;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "Oxygen &#2321;&#2325;&#2381;&#2360;&#2368;&#2332;&#2344;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Oxygen</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2321;&#2325;&#2381;&#2360;&#2368;&#2332;&#2344;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "Ammonia &#2309;&#2350;&#2379;&#2344;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Ammonia</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2309;&#2350;&#2379;&#2344;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "Methane &#2350;&#2368;&#2341;&#2375;&#2344;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Methane</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2350;&#2368;&#2341;&#2375;&#2344;</span>"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "A",
      "solution": "<p>When iron reacts with water, it forms iron oxide (rust) and hydrogen gas:</p><p>3Fe+4H2O&rarr;Fe3O4+4H23Fe + 4H_2O &rarr; Fe_3O_4 + 4H_23Fe+4H2&#8203;O&rarr;Fe3&#8203;O4&#8203;+4H2&#8203;</p><p>This reaction takes place in the presence of steam at high temperatures. Hydrogen gas is released as a byproduct.</p>",
      "images": [],
      "subject": null,
      "topic": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
    {
      "id": "cb6f94d2a511-q9",
      "number": 9,
      "question": "Which of the following decomposition reactions is NOT a redox reaction? Options: &#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344; &#2360;&#2368; &#2309;&#2346;&#2328;&#2335;&#2344; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2352;&#2375;&#2337;&#2377;&#2325;&#2381;&#2360; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2344;&#2361;&#2368;&#2306; &#2361;&#2376;? &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2354;&#2381;&#2346;:",
      "questionHtml": "<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Which of the following decomposition reactions is NOT a redox reaction?</p><p><b>Options:</b></p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344; &#2360;&#2368; &#2309;&#2346;&#2328;&#2335;&#2344; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2352;&#2375;&#2337;&#2377;&#2325;&#2381;&#2360; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2344;&#2361;&#2368;&#2306; &#2361;&#2376;?</p><p><b>&#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2354;&#2381;&#2346;:</b></span>",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "Decomposition of dihydrogen monoxide &#2337;&#2366;&#2311;&#2361;&#2366;&#2311;&#2337;&#2381;&#2352;&#2379;&#2332;&#2344; &#2350;&#2379;&#2344;&#2379;&#2321;&#2325;&#2381;&#2360;&#2366;&#2311;&#2337; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2346;&#2328;&#2335;&#2344;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Decomposition of dihydrogen monoxide</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2337;&#2366;&#2311;&#2361;&#2366;&#2311;&#2337;&#2381;&#2352;&#2379;&#2332;&#2344; &#2350;&#2379;&#2344;&#2379;&#2321;&#2325;&#2381;&#2360;&#2366;&#2311;&#2337; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2346;&#2328;&#2335;&#2344;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "Decomposition of sodium hydride &#2360;&#2379;&#2337;&#2367;&#2351;&#2350; &#2361;&#2366;&#2311;&#2337;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2311;&#2337; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2346;&#2328;&#2335;&#2344;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Decomposition of sodium hydride</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2360;&#2379;&#2337;&#2367;&#2351;&#2350; &#2361;&#2366;&#2311;&#2337;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2311;&#2337; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2346;&#2328;&#2335;&#2344;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "Decomposition of potassium chlorate &#2346;&#2379;&#2335;&#2375;&#2358;&#2367;&#2351;&#2350; &#2325;&#2381;&#2354;&#2379;&#2352;&#2375;&#2335; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2346;&#2328;&#2335;&#2344;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Decomposition of potassium chlorate</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2346;&#2379;&#2335;&#2375;&#2358;&#2367;&#2351;&#2350; &#2325;&#2381;&#2354;&#2379;&#2352;&#2375;&#2335; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2346;&#2328;&#2335;&#2344;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "Decomposition of calcium carbonate &#2325;&#2376;&#2354;&#2381;&#2358;&#2367;&#2351;&#2350; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2348;&#2379;&#2344;&#2375;&#2335; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2346;&#2328;&#2335;&#2344;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Decomposition of calcium carbonate</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2325;&#2376;&#2354;&#2381;&#2358;&#2367;&#2351;&#2350; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2348;&#2379;&#2344;&#2375;&#2335; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2346;&#2328;&#2335;&#2344;</span>"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "D",
      "solution": "<p>1) <b>What is a Redox Reaction?</b></p><p>o A redox (reduction-oxidation) reaction involves the transfer of electrons, where one substance is oxidized (loses electrons) and another is reduced (gains electrons).</p><p>2) <b>Analysis of the Options:</b></p><p>o <b>Dihydrogen monoxide (water):</b> 2H<sub>2</sub>O&rarr;2H<sub>2</sub>+O<sub>2</sub>&#8203; (Redox reaction as hydrogen is reduced and oxygen is oxidized).</p><p>o <b>Sodium hydride:</b> 2NaH&rarr;2Na+H<sub>2</sub> &#8203; (Redox reaction as sodium is oxidized and hydrogen is reduced).</p><p>o <b>Potassium chlorate:</b> 2KClO3&rarr;2KCl+3O<sub>2</sub>&#8203; (Redox reaction as oxygen is reduced and potassium is oxidized).</p><p>o <b>Calcium carbonate:</b> CaCO3&rarr;CaO+CO<sub>2</sub>&#8203; (NOT a redox reaction, as no electrons are transferred).</p><p>Thus, the correct answer is <b>Decomposition of calcium carbonate</b>.</p>",
      "images": [],
      "subject": null,
      "topic": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
    {
      "id": "cb6f94d2a511-q10",
      "number": 10,
      "question": "When a magnesium ribbon is burnt in oxygen, it gets converted to _____. &#2332;&#2348; &#2319;&#2325; &#2350;&#2376;&#2327;&#2381;&#2344;&#2368;&#2358;&#2367;&#2351;&#2350; &#2352;&#2367;&#2348;&#2344; &#2325;&#2379; &#2321;&#2325;&#2381;&#2360;&#2368;&#2332;&#2344; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2332;&#2354;&#2366;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2351;&#2361; _____ &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2367;&#2340; &#2361;&#2379; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;",
      "questionHtml": "<span class=\"eqt\"><p>When a magnesium ribbon is burnt in oxygen, it gets converted to _____.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2332;&#2348; &#2319;&#2325; &#2350;&#2376;&#2327;&#2381;&#2344;&#2368;&#2358;&#2367;&#2351;&#2350; &#2352;&#2367;&#2348;&#2344; &#2325;&#2379; &#2321;&#2325;&#2381;&#2360;&#2368;&#2332;&#2344; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2332;&#2354;&#2366;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2351;&#2361; _____ &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2367;&#2340; &#2361;&#2379; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;</p></span>",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "Magnesium peroxide &#2350;&#2376;&#2327;&#2381;&#2344;&#2368;&#2358;&#2367;&#2351;&#2350; &#2346;&#2375;&#2352;&#2379;&#2325;&#2381;&#2360;&#2366;&#2311;&#2337;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Magnesium peroxide</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2350;&#2376;&#2327;&#2381;&#2344;&#2368;&#2358;&#2367;&#2351;&#2350; &#2346;&#2375;&#2352;&#2379;&#2325;&#2381;&#2360;&#2366;&#2311;&#2337;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "Magnesium hydroxide &#2350;&#2376;&#2327;&#2381;&#2344;&#2375;&#2358;&#2367;&#2351;&#2350; &#2361;&#2366;&#2351;&#2337;&#2381;&#2352;&#2377;&#2325;&#2381;&#2360;&#2366;&#2311;&#2337;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Magnesium hydroxide</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2350;&#2376;&#2327;&#2381;&#2344;&#2375;&#2358;&#2367;&#2351;&#2350; &#2361;&#2366;&#2351;&#2337;&#2381;&#2352;&#2377;&#2325;&#2381;&#2360;&#2366;&#2311;&#2337;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "Magnesium carbonate &#2350;&#2376;&#2327;&#2381;&#2344;&#2368;&#2358;&#2367;&#2351;&#2350; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2348;&#2379;&#2344;&#2375;&#2335;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Magnesium carbonate</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2350;&#2376;&#2327;&#2381;&#2344;&#2368;&#2358;&#2367;&#2351;&#2350; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2348;&#2379;&#2344;&#2375;&#2335;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "Magnesium oxide &#2350;&#2376;&#2327;&#2381;&#2344;&#2368;&#2358;&#2367;&#2351;&#2350; &#2321;&#2325;&#2381;&#2360;&#2366;&#2311;&#2337;",
          "html": "<span class=\"eqt\">Magnesium oxide</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2350;&#2376;&#2327;&#2381;&#2344;&#2368;&#2358;&#2367;&#2351;&#2350; &#2321;&#2325;&#2381;&#2360;&#2366;&#2311;&#2337;</span>"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "D",
      "solution": "<p>When a magnesium ribbon is burnt in oxygen, it gets converted to <b>magnesium oxide</b>. The substances that undergo chemical change in the reaction, magnesium and oxygen, are the reactants. The new substance is magnesium oxide, formed during the reaction, as a product.</p>",
